---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "I'm a starter theme for Astro.build",
	title: "Me",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-5">Me</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			i’m a 24-year-old software developer and HCI master's student focused on the human-computer
			relationship. i'm a strong advocate for local AI, believing that integrating LLMs directly
			onto user devices should enhance user experience without compromising privacy or the
			environment.
		</p>
		<p>
			professionally, i have over a year of experience leading the development of an AI chatbot
			framework integrated with internal codebases and enterprise documentation. i also co-authored
			an IEEE-featured research paper on software-defined networks during my undergrad.
		</p>

		<h3 class="subtitle mt-6 mb-2">You can read my paper here ↓</h3>
		<a
			class="inline-block text-green-600 underline transition-colors hover:text-white"
			href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10127564/citations?tabFilter=papers#citations"
			rel="noreferrer"
			target="_blank"
		>
			Threats to Control Plane of Software Defined Networks: An Extensive Study
		</a>

		<h3 class="subtitle mb-4">Core Stack</h3>
		<p>
			i try not to get boxed into a single ecosystem, but javascript/typescript and python are
			definitely my bread and butter.
		</p>
		<ul class="list-inside list-disc" role="list">
			<li><strong>Frontend / Mobile:</strong> next.js, react native (expo)</li>
			<li><strong>Backend / DBs:</strong> fastAPI, node.js, express, mongodb, postgres, and sql</li>
			<li><strong>Data / ML:</strong> python</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 class="subtitle mb-4">When I'm Not Coding</h3>
		<p>you can usually find me playing age of empires, chess or at a trivia night!</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
